course: dictionary
lesson: 12255
title: One word, four meanings: consume
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Consume is a formal word, so you will meet it in books, science and news. It has four main meanings: to eat or drink something, to use up fuel, energy, time or money, to destroy something completely, as fire does, and to be full of a strong feeling.
explain: To choose the right meaning, look at the words around it. «The hungry dog consumed its whole bowl in seconds.» The bowl tells you it means ate. «The fire consumed the wooden barn.» The fire tells you it means destroyed. Always ask: what word would fit here?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If «ate» makes the sentence make sense, you have found it. If it does not, try another meaning from the list until one fits.
fact: «Consume» is a formal word for eat or drink.
fact: «Consume» can also mean to use up fuel, energy, time or money, as in «The old car consumes a lot of petrol.»
fact: «Consumed» can mean destroyed completely, as fire does to a building.
fact: «Consumed with» means full of a strong feeling, as in «She was consumed with jealousy.»
fact: In science, animals that eat plants are called primary consumers, and «time-consuming» means it takes a lot of time.
exercise: «The hungry dog consumed its whole bowl in seconds.» What does consumed mean here? | Washed it clean | Looked at it carefully | *Ate it all up
exercise: «The old car consumes a lot of petrol.» What does the car use up? | The driver's hat | *Petrol | The road
exercise: «Rabbits are primary consumers, because they eat plants.» What does consumers mean in this science sentence? | *Animals that eat plants or other food | Plants that grow in the sun | Machines that make petrol | Rocks in a river
test: «The fire consumed the wooden barn in an hour.» What does consumed mean here? | Painted bright red | *Destroyed completely | Built again | Cooled down slowly
test: «He was consumed with jealousy when his friend won the prize.» What does consumed with mean here? | *Filled completely by a strong feeling | Bored of the game | Tired after running | Too shy to speak
exam: Mum says, «Homework is very time-consuming tonight.» What does time-consuming mean? | Is fun to do early | Makes time go backwards | Costs no money at all | *Takes a lot of time
